From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:19:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09847/11362] [outer-loop] Correct the live-corpus entry: my
 scan swept two repo clones

Corrects d1734d51fc, committed under an hour earlier. The prior text is kept
verbatim; this is appended beside it.

WRONG: 2.6% live, 2212-row corpus, and "llm_on_row_valid overstates live
coverage by ~19x".

CAUSE: the scan globbed $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/**/rows*.json. 180 of 195 matched
files were inside abpin/ and headwt/, two byte-identical clones of this repo in
the scratch tree, contributing 9,250 raw rows. The apparent 1,131-row
early_stop_sweep_20260726 is not in the scratch tree at all -- it lives in
results/ and the glob reached it only through the clones. So the thing I set out
to check, whether anything aggregated across early_stop_sweep as live, was
chasing an artifact of my own scan.

CORRECTED, clone-excluded and deduplicated by (run, game, seed, arm): 86 rows,
47 token-producing, 42 both valid and token-producing, and ZERO rows that are
valid with no tokens. llm_on_row_valid is a sound live filter. The 19x
overstatement does not exist.

WHAT STANDS, and is starker than before: the live corpus is ~47 rows total.
baseline25 24, seedsweep 11, supab 5, fixrun 3, supab3 2, supab2_VOID_oom 1,
supab5 1. Today's sweep is about a quarter of all live data the project has.
Two game-specific patterns were claimed today from this base; both were wrong.

WHY THIS ONE MATTERS BEYOND THE NUMBERS. It is the same clone-duplication that
corrupted scripts/arc_induction_quality.py, diagnosed and written up earlier
today, with a memory entry I wrote myself. I read that write-up, repeated the
error within hours, and committed the result to memory and known-issues before
catching it. Prose did not prevent the recurrence. The scorer's nested-clone
refusal (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6700) would have. That is the step-6 argument in CLAUDE.md
demonstrated on its own author: a lesson recorded as prose costs every future
reader a memory; a lesson converted into a check costs nothing and cannot be
forgotten.

Any new corpus scan over the scratch tree must exclude nested clones explicitly
or reuse a scanner that already does.

Memory project_live_llm_corpus_is_tiny rewritten with the corrected numbers and
the failure mode.

